  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan ACM floods 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavy rains since May this year, combined with overflowing Lake Victoria have caused severe flooding in large parts of South Sudan. South Sudan is experiencing multiple crises including these unprecedented levels of floods, an influx of returnees and refugees because of the conflict in Sudan, severe food insecurity and hyperinflation. The rainy season has become increasingly severe due to climate change, stretching communities&#x2019; ability to cope with the devastation, and in some cases causing permanent displacement of communities.  This action prioritises the five Payams in Fangak County by providing Cash for Food to the most vulnerable households in line with cluster recommendations in Manajang, Pulita and Barboui payams and provide Shelter NFIs to households in need of shelter in Pulita, Mareang and Paguir Payams.</narrative>
  </description>
